	(text "PWR_GOOD: four open-drain comparators share the pull-up R51, so the line is\nhigh only while all four rails are present. R41, R43 and R44 set the\nthresholds: 0.9001 x +3V3_C = 2.970 V and 0.4985 x +3V3_C = 1.645 V.\nTrip levels (calculated): +3V3_A 2.97 V, +12V_A 9.85 V, -4V_A -2.57 V, VREF 2.245 V.\nHigh level 0.82 x +3V3_C (R51 with R52); R52 holds the line low without supply.\nStart (simulated): 5V_OK enables +3V3_C and +3V3_A, then -4V_A (0.3 ms), +12V_A\n(8 ms to 17 ms), VREF and PWR_GOOD (about 24 ms). +13V5 is up before 5V_OK."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 144.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "57f9c301-3e01-5a05-8b2d-ebceb6013109")
	)
	(text "C32, C33 and C34 keep an edge of PWR_GOOD from moving the thresholds through\nthe pin capacitance of the package: each output pin of U14 is the neighbor of\nan inverting input (time constants 9 us, 25 us and 36 us, calculated)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 163.83 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f0f314f3-04a5-5ff8-9e83-aa80fb1b057f")
	)
